## Changing cluster IP addresses

### Updating the IP of worker node

A worker node deployed by kubeadm only has a kubelet running and no control plane components.
To update the IP of such a worker node host, first you need to establish if the kubelet
was configured with a custom `--node-ip` flag. This flag allows overriding what IPv4/IPv6
addresses will be used for this node in the cluster. If the flag is not provided the kubelet
will try to detect
[usable IPs from default routes](/docs/setup/production-environment/tools/kubeadm/create-cluster-kubeadm/#network-setup)
on the host.

To check if `--node-ip` is used try to find it in the file `/var/lib/kubelet/kubeadm-flags.env`.
Normally this flag would come from `JoinConfiguration.nodeRegistration.kubeletExtraArgs` when
your are calling `kubeadm join`.

### If the flag is used

- Make sure the node is first drained. Execute the command `kubectl drain <worker-node-name>`
- Edit `/var/lib/kubelet/kubeadm-flags.env` and place a new value after `--node-ip`.
- Call `systemctl restart kubelet`.

